==Battleground==
*1 [[Bore]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Bakoo]] spawns as the boss.
**2 [[Bore]]s spawn, delay 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
**20 [[Wall Doge]]s spawn, delay 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
**1 [[Kang Roo]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Assuming you've followed the [[Honey Trap (Deadly) (Queen & Maiden)#Strategy|advice]] for the previous stage, you should have an [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red]] and [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]] units in your lineup. Simply control the Bore, stack Long Distance units, and then sit back and watch total Bakoo destruction.

==Trivia==
*Bombergirl's seemingly arbitrary name is a pun that only works in Japanese. The Japanese word for bomb, ''bakudan'', happens to contain the word ''baku'', which can refer to either a [[wikipedia:Malayan tapir|Malayan tapir]], or a [[wikipedia:Baku (mythology)|dream-eating mythical creature]], both of which served as inspirations for [[Bakoo]].

